The drill finished with 12 of 12 questions passing after 2 iterations. The one first-pass failure was `pe21-2b`.

- **Iteration 1:** 11 of 12 passed. `pe21-2b` failed on a wording gap. It says "find an estimator for the parameter θ", and the old sheet only said "MLE" or "maximum likelihood", so the persona couldn't connect them.
- **Rewrite:** I added a trigger line with the exam's own phrases ("derive the MLE", "determine the maximum likelihood estimate", "find an estimator for θ"). I also added the likelihood L = ∏p and a worked example with the x/(2θ) prefactor, which also covers the x/θ case. To make room I dropped the cos/sin derivative rules, the "Gaussian" remark and some intermediate steps.
- **Iteration 2:** I re-solved only `pe21-2b` with the new sheet and it passed.

I couldn't count characters exactly, so the sheet is only estimated at about 2200, against the 2245 hard cap. If it is over, drop the "Exponent −x²/θ" clause and the "(e.g. ln x)" note.

Two passes were judgement calls. `jun26-2b` passed because the "mean ÷ k stages" note covers the "explain" part. `nov22-2d` passed because the sheet gives the angle result directly, without showing the step to tan⁻¹.

Nothing is out of scope. I didn't commit or push the files, and the progress log was rewritten whole rather than appended to, because I had no append tool.

